# 4. CANONICAL TASK SYSTEM

Tasks are different from calendar events.

A task is an actual actionable record.

A calendar event can be a projection of a task, but not every calendar event must be a task.

For example:

- A predicted crop-stage milestone is an event.
- A weather-driven recommended irrigation window is an event or recommendation projection.
- A farmer-created reminder is a task.
- A confirmed soil sampling operation may be a task linked to a soil-testing workflow.

Do not create a task for every displayed calendar event.

## 4.1 Task ownership

All task creation and mutation must use one canonical Task entity.

If the project already has a task model, extend or adapt it rather than introducing a second independent task system.

### Recommended task fields

```text
Task
----
id
farm_id
field_id
created_by
assigned_to
title
description
task_type
priority
status

scheduled_start
scheduled_end
due_date
timezone

source_type
source_id

linked_rotation_plan_id
