linked_observation_id

reminder_at
reminder_status

created_at
updated_at
completed_at
completed_by

deferred_until
cancelled_at

version
```

Use nullable relationships for genuinely optional links.

Use actual foreign keys and validation where the database supports them.

Store the task's timezone explicitly.

Do not use the event title as a unique identifier.

## 4.2 Task types

Support the relevant task types:

- Planting.
- Harvesting.
- Irrigation.
- Soil testing.
- Scouting.
- Fertilizer.
- Rotation preparation.
- Crop review.
- Deep Analysis review.
- Farmer-defined task.
- General reminder.

The type list must remain compatible with the existing domain model.

## 4.3 Task status

Use a controlled status system:

```text
open
scheduled
in_progress
completed
deferred
cancelled
```

Not every task type needs every status.

Do not invent status transitions that the existing workflow cannot support.

## 4.4 Task state transitions

Valid examples:

```text
open -> in_progress
open -> completed
open -> deferred
open -> cancelled

scheduled -> in_progress
scheduled -> completed
scheduled -> deferred
scheduled -> cancelled

in_progress -> completed
in_progress -> deferred
```

Rescheduling changes the scheduled date or due window without erasing history.

A completed task must not become open just because a model recalculates a future recommendation.

Reopening a task, if supported, must be an explicit audited action.

