## 7.1 Provenance

Every event must indicate how its date was obtained.

Use explicit provenance labels:

| Basis | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Planned | Part of an approved or saved plan |
| Scheduled | Explicitly scheduled by a farmer or workflow |
| Modelled | Calculated estimate or prediction |
| Observed | Recorded actual observation |
| Completed | Reported completed operation |

Do not display a modelled date as a confirmed event.

Do not display a planned operation as something that has already occurred.

## 7.2 Date windows

Agricultural recommendations are often date windows rather than exact dates.

For example:

```text
Recommended planting window:
November 18–24
```

Do not reduce this to an invented exact date.

Represent the start and end separately.

The calendar may show the range visually across relevant dates.

The right-side activity panel should communicate the full date window.

