# 12. RIGHT-HAND TODAY'S ACTIVITIES PANEL — BACKEND LOGIC

The right-hand panel is not a manually populated static list.

It is a filtered, grouped and prioritized projection of the selected date.

It should contain the following sections:

## 12.1 Crops and stages

Retrieve active crop-stage information relevant to the selected date.

Display:
- Crop.
- Field.
- Growth stage.
- Stage basis.
- Relevant status.
- Link to crop/rotation details.

## 12.2 Planned work

Display upcoming operations and recommendations that apply to the selected date.

Examples:
- Irrigation.
- Rotation preparation.
- Fertilizer application.
- Planting preparation.

Each row must preserve whether it is a planned action or a modelled recommendation.

## 12.3 Tasks due

Retrieve canonical tasks whose due window includes the selected date.

Display:
- Title.
- Field.
- Priority.
- Status.
- Due time/window.
- Action controls.

Completed tasks should not appear as open work.

They may be shown in a separate completed section or historical detail view.

## 12.4 Observations

Retrieve farmer-recorded observations relevant to the selected date.

Examples:
- Pest observation.
- Crop condition observation.
- Soil condition record.
- Actual field operation.

Do not represent a historical observation as a future task.

## 12.5 Next 7 Days

Calculate the seven-day window using the selected farm's timezone.

Return actual upcoming tasks and relevant projected milestones.

Sort chronologically.

Use a clearly defined start and end boundary.

Do not accidentally include the same event twice if it is already represented through more than one linked source.

## 12.6 Empty date behaviour

If the selected date has no activities:

Display an honest empty state:

"No activities scheduled for this date."

Offer:
"Add a task"

Do not insert artificial events just to make the panel look populated.

