# 13. MONTH, AGENDA AND TIMELINE VIEWS

The backend should support the different calendar views through the same event-projection architecture.

## 13.1 Month view

Retrieve events covering the full displayed calendar range.

Include the preceding and following dates needed to render complete weeks.

Respect the selected farm's locale and timezone.

## 13.2 Agenda view

Return upcoming events in chronological order.

Support a one-to-two-week window and allow the user to extend it.

## 13.3 Timeline view

Return supported events across the selected period with:
- Start date.
- End date.
- Farm.
- Field.
- Event type.
- Provenance.
- Status.

Do not invent start/end durations for events that only have one known date.

## 13.4 Multi-field overlay

Support multiple field events on the same calendar.

Different farms and fields must remain distinguishable even when the crop name and date are identical.

Always display farm/field labels.

