# 17. DATABASE AND DATA INTEGRITY REQUIREMENTS

Inspect the existing database before adding tables.

Only add genuinely missing structures.

Potential additional structures include:

- Calendar projection metadata.
- Task audit records, if no equivalent exists.
- Domain event outbox, if no equivalent exists.
- Reminder delivery records, if no equivalent exists.
- Calendar synchronization cursors, if needed.

Do not create a new copy of:
- Farms.
- Fields.
- Crop records.
- Rotation plans.
- Irrigation records.
- Soil reports.
- Scouting records.
- Tasks.

## 17.1 Database constraints

Implement:
- Foreign keys.
- Appropriate indexes.
- Unique idempotency keys.
- Valid status constraints.
- Valid date windows.
- Version control.
- Authorization checks.

Useful indexes may include:

```text
(farm_id, start_date)
(field_id, start_date)
(task_id, status)
(source_type, source_id)
(user_id, idempotency_key)
```

Adapt the exact indexes to the existing schema and query patterns.

## 17.2 Transactions

Task creation, updates and important state changes should use database transactions.

An audit record must not be missing because an update succeeded while the audit write failed.

For domain-event publication, use the transactional outbox approach where supported.

