# 18. NOTIFICATIONS AND REMINDERS

The calendar may offer reminders for user-created tasks.

Reminder scheduling must be based on actual task data.

Support:
- Reminder time.
- Reminder timezone.
- Delivery status.
- Retry state.
- Delivery timestamp.

Do not show Google Calendar, Outlook or other external synchronization controls unless the integrations actually exist.

Do not claim a reminder was delivered merely because it was scheduled.

Keep notification delivery separate from calendar event creation.

If a task is rescheduled, update its pending reminder.

If it is cancelled or completed, prevent obsolete pending reminders from being delivered where possible.

