# 22. PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS

The calendar must remain fast even when a farm has many fields and years of historical records.

Implement:

- Date-range queries.
- Indexed source lookups.
- Pagination for large agenda results.
- Incremental synchronization where appropriate.
- Projection caching.
- Batch retrieval from source services.
- Avoidance of N+1 database queries.
- Lazy loading of detailed evidence.
- Efficient event grouping.

Do not load every historical farm event just to render the current month.

The calendar should retrieve the selected month and only the additional data needed for the visible upcoming section.

